{
  "description": "The Legend rows Python draws for the content and skew tracks of a request with explicit track slots (gbdraw/diagrams/circular/assemble.py::_sync_legend_table_for_circular_slots, gbdraw/diagrams/linear/assemble.py::_sync_legend_table_for_linear_slots), each as [key, palette key of its fill, the slot that draws it (null: no explicit slot), fill]. `palette` gives the gc_content, skew_high and skew_low colors of the Generate. Python's answer is the keys and fills, in order (tests/test_legend_row_facts.py); the Web app's is the slot, the palette key and the fill it reads for each key (services/track-legend-rows.js::trackLegendRows, tests/web/track-legend-row-colors.test.mjs). The rows of a request without explicit slots are in legend_generated_rows.json.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "circular: a GC skew slot and an AT skew slot with its own colors and label",
      "mode": "circular",
      "dinucleotide": "GC",
      "palette": {"gc_content": "#8daf38", "skew_high": "#f6a8f1", "skew_low": "#bd96df"},
      "slots": [
        {"id": "features", "renderer": "features", "enabled": true, "params": {"lane_direction": "split"}},
        {"id": "gc_content", "renderer": "dinucleotide_content", "enabled": true, "params": {}},
        {"id": "gc_skew", "renderer": "dinucleotide_skew", "enabled": true, "params": {}},
        {"id": "a_skew_2", "renderer": "dinucleotide_skew", "enabled": true, "params": {"nt": "AT", "positive_color": "#deaf6e", "negative_color": "#7294e3", "legend_label": "AT skew"}},
        {"id": "ticks", "renderer": "ticks", "enabled": true, "params": {}}
      ],
      "rows": [
        ["GC content", "gc_content", "gc_content", "#8daf38"],
        ["GC skew (+)", "skew_high", "gc_skew", "#f6a8f1"],
        ["GC skew (-)", "skew_low", "gc_skew", "#bd96df"],
        ["AT skew (+)", "skew_high", "a_skew_2", "#deaf6e"],
        ["AT skew (-)", "skew_low", "a_skew_2", "#7294e3"]
      ]
    },
